              "id": "CVE-2026-34040",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Moby: Moby: Authorization bypass vulnerability"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Moby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows attackers to bypass authorization plugins (AuthZ). This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34040",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-34040\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/docker/docker\nFixed Version: 29.3.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-34040](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34040)\nMoby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows attackers to bypass authorization plugins (AuthZ). This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-34040**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/docker/docker|29.3.1|[CVE-2026-34040](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34040)|\n\nMoby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows attackers to bypass authorization plugins (AuthZ). This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1."
              },
